[{:db/id "q-32133/selection/02a91403cf586768ea092ffb64b2f8be222f8d3f9c272262b0679bc67d14eb89" :answer/id #uuid "de3c6e94-f543-5c16-98f0-1e3146f7eff8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32133/selection/6323fe987b03c285af6c9909a1eabb548540ac9543e0b3e857bb5fe2414ba7f3" :answer/id #uuid "53bc419f-611d-5b57-a773-9650534b20d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32133/selection/b3678a107204c63485845708ad5eb7ed435275c7f2a17f623aace468138eff2c" :answer/id #uuid "79e6fec9-212a-5eaf-973f-1ef5080c6860" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32133/selection/2bf5185c6fd1831c84897fd6774130c74bb4792dd23231a300440d92913e4256" :answer/id #uuid "c8e61017-63c1-5e69-9922-3c3eea3a6b3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32133/selection/73928427f85ebaa1cba7f8f08471b9e7486d842d2ef604fc97f10d42f631c5f1" :answer/id #uuid "ca300e7e-9d7a-53b6-8c3e-72568609817e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32133/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe03e7ec-d1e6-5682-8944-61e7a8fa8b03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32133/selection/73928427f85ebaa1cba7f8f08471b9e7486d842d2ef604fc97f10d42f631c5f1" :answer-field/choices ["q-32133/selection/02a91403cf586768ea092ffb64b2f8be222f8d3f9c272262b0679bc67d14eb89" "q-32133/selection/6323fe987b03c285af6c9909a1eabb548540ac9543e0b3e857bb5fe2414ba7f3" "q-32133/selection/b3678a107204c63485845708ad5eb7ed435275c7f2a17f623aace468138eff2c" "q-32133/selection/2bf5185c6fd1831c84897fd6774130c74bb4792dd23231a300440d92913e4256" "q-32133/selection/73928427f85ebaa1cba7f8f08471b9e7486d842d2ef604fc97f10d42f631c5f1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32133" :question/id #uuid "324f3608-babb-59d3-b059-1a5e8e0a8c0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-32133" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32133/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32133"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32144/selection/d7450e12a5b011bc58a6c4ff3f08d24f50987818ef28fa62ebbcab5d8150c25b" :answer/id #uuid "e82552f9-aff8-5120-a48a-fdc512cc5268" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{3}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32144/selection/9372275c0968b4e1153a6d501ad425813774ff862cd02ec68aff79d67b5ad0ce" :answer/id #uuid "2812978b-c78b-5d62-838c-36ef550a0191" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32144/selection/8c19085afa9fe9b766e7687f108c64017a81982e2e5842f87990f2dc13548458" :answer/id #uuid "0f18f460-1c27-5557-8873-b95a771f09ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32144/selection/6e445ab8fb9d182ed299502f1abe52756a78391436b88bbe6ae54c9c5b59b8e2" :answer/id #uuid "fa7b5670-0364-5c37-9421-f7307e045b0e" :answer/type :answer.